From 8d43ac9bcf351ef1d526e0f6f0a3b2c9713d6001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-d-robotics maintainers <maintainers@invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 03:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dm-fdekey: validate delimiter before applying offset

The RDKOS 3.5.0 source tests `tmp + 1` after strstr().  Pointer
arithmetic cannot make a null pointer non-null, so current GCC correctly
diagnoses the condition as always true when CONFIG_WERROR is enabled.

Test the strstr() result before incrementing it.  This preserves the
intended error path for a key string without its ':' delimiter and keeps
the vendor warning policy intact.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 drivers/md/dm-fdekey.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/md/dm-fdekey.c b/drivers/md/dm-fdekey.c
index 6ff3d22f4e36..75e9e00fd42f 100644
--- a/drivers/md/dm-fdekey.c
+++ b/drivers/md/dm-fdekey.c
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@ static int handle_key(unsigned char *key, char *dr_key)
 	int ret;
 
 	tmp = strstr(key, ":");
-	if (! (tmp + 1)) {
+	if (!tmp) {
 		return -1;
 	}
 	tmp += 1;
-- 
2.43.0
